## 2 · Authority — who wins on a conflict

```
brief  >  reality  >  decision  >  blueprint  >  reference
```

| Tier | Files | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **brief** | `BRIEF-01`…`BRIEF-07`, `BRIEF-09` | What the assignment demands. External, non-negotiable. If anything contradicts it, the other thing is wrong. |
| **reality** | `BUILD-01`, `BUILD-02`, `BUILD-03` | What actually exists/holds right now. |
| **decision** | `DEC-01` | The decision register: the settled concept stated as fact, and the items still open. |
| **blueprint** | *(none yet)* | `DES-xx`/`DATA-xx` appear when the SwiftUI build starts; until then design and content answers come from `.claude/data-design/`. |
| **reference** | `REF-01`, `REF-02` | Supporting material. Never overrides anything. |

**When you spot a conflict:** answer from the higher tier, then say the lower-tier file is stale and name it. Do not silently reconcile.

---

## 3 · Invariants

The product, process and phase invariants live in **`CLAUDE.md` § Invariants — never violate** —
the kernel that is always loaded alongside this rule. They are not restated here: one copy, one
place to keep true.


## 4 · Keeping the KB true

Any change must be reflected in the KB in the same turn:

| Change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| A decision closes (concept, roles, names, stack…) | `DEC-01` (state it as a fact — no date, no decision history; the register keeps only what *is*) → `BUILD-01` → seed `DES-xx`/`DATA-xx` when design begins |
| Project/repo state changes (repo cloned, Xcode project created, code written) | `BUILD-01` |
| The plan changes or a milestone passes | `BUILD-02` |
| A meeting happens | `BUILD-03` (retire/replace the agenda) + `DEC-01` |
| A file added, moved or removed | frontmatter + `.claude/context-index.md` §1–2 + the `CLAUDE.md` router |

**A KB that silently drifts is worse than no KB** — it converts uncertainty into confident error. If you cannot verify a "reality" claim, say so rather than repeating it.
